          "id": "madronich_column_j_lev40",
          "description": "END-TO-END: the 21 photolysis frequencies RADM2 reads, computed from the COLUMN STATE through the mounted optical-depth and two-stream components, against the WRF-Chem 4.8 em_scm_xy reference (chem_opt = 101 RADM2 KPP, phot_opt = 1 Madronich; 37.6 N 96.7 W, 1999-10-22 19:00 UTC start; GNU gfortran 13.3 REAL*4; run directory data/eqwefic/chem_scm_phot; dumped by the ctessum-claude/WRF fork, branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem, at call 1410, radiative-transfer level 40). The column at this call is completely CLEAR, so the RT grid is the plain 70-interface extended grid and trapez's interpolation back onto the model levels is the identity for levels 1..60. NOTHING ABOUT THE RADIATION FIELD IS SUPPLIED HERE: the layer optical depths, the delta-Eddington scaling, the spherical slant paths, the direct beam and the full 138-unknown tridiagonal two-stream solve are all computed by the two mounted components from the layer columns. Only the cross sections and quantum yields arrive as data, and those are pinned separately by MadronichSpectra. Expected values are phot1_s, which the instrumented fork verified equals jv(1:21) of the RADM2 integrator to 1.1e-7 relative across four model times -- so dumps/radm2_wrf/*.json is an INDEPENDENT second check on these numbers, not the same data twice. Single-precision reference; tolerance rel 1e-3, which is what a single-precision two-stream solve over 138 unknowns per bin supports.",
