        {
          "id": "madronich_column_j_full",
          "description": "THE WHOLE COLUMN: all 21 photolysis frequencies at all 59 WRF model levels, computed from the column state through the mounted optical-depth and two-stream components, against the WRF-Chem 4.8 em_scm_xy reference (chem_opt = 101 RADM2 KPP, phot_opt = 1 Madronich; clear column, call 1410; GNU gfortran 13.3 REAL*4; data/eqwefic/chem_scm_phot; ctessum-claude/WRF fork, branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem). This is the full jv(1:21) block the RADM2 integrator consumes -- the thing that arrived as an INPUT in the dumps this project started from, now computed. Levels 1..59 are the model levels; the RT grid carries ten more above the model top, which WRF never exports. SIZE, measured: the sigma_qy_col array is 21 x 70 x 101 = 148,470 numbers, 1.72 MB of JSON, which puts this file at about 1.9 MB -- the same order as the 1.19 MB fastjx_interp_troposphere.esm already in EarthSciModels. It is reference DATA in a test block, not model logic. It could be halved by splitting the 12 level-independent channels from the 9 that vary, and removed entirely by a column-shaped spectra component -- but that would mean writing MadronichSpectra's eleven spectra a second time in 2-D form. Single-precision reference; rel 1e-3, which is what a single-precision two-stream solve over 138 unknowns per bin supports.",
